 {"id": "RELEASE-LORE-004", "title": "[P2] Repo ships no release tooling or release docs: no Makefile/Dockerfile/goreleaser/scripts/release*, no docs/RELEASE.md, and ci.yml never fires on tags — every cut would be hand-rolled", "status": "complete", "priority": "P2", "phase": "release", "repo": "https://github.com/get-h3/lore", "created_at": "2026-09-29T05:30:20Z", "updated_at": "2026-09-30T00:52:57Z", "detail": "Releng doctrine (fleet): a project should ship its own release script + release docs, and the tag path should be gated by CI. lore ships neither. Inventory at origin/main 88245fd: no Makefile, no Dockerfile, no .goreleaser.yml, no scripts/release*, no docs/RELEASE*.md (docs/ = INSTALL.md, PRD.md, RUNBOOK-STORE.md, acceptance/, dogfood/); .github/workflows/ci.yml triggers on `push: branches:[main]` and `pull_request` only — it never fires on tags, so a tag push is unverified by CI and there is no version-authority / changelog-drift gate to catch a tag/version mismatch. CHANGELOG.md is the only release-adjacent artifact and it carries an explicit 'Not released: no tag, no publish' note for 0.1.2. ACCEPTANCE: (1) a release script (e.g. scripts/release.sh) that refuses a dirty tree, refuses a red CI sha, refuses an existing tag, derives the tag from the version stamp, and tags + creates the Release object + verifies `gh release view`; (2) docs/RELEASE.md naming the tag namespace, the version-stamp files, the changelog promotion rule and the rollback path (previous tag); (3) a tag-triggered CI job asserting `pyproject.toml version == lore.__version__ == the newest numeric CHANGELOG heading == the tag`. Prerequisite for RELEASE-LORE-003 leg (c).", "reasoning": "tick lore-releng-2026-09-29-05-20-09 inventory sweep at origin/main 88245fd: `ls` of the repo root, `find -maxdepth 2` for Dockerfile*/goreleaser/Makefile/release*, `ls docs/`, and `grep -n 'version|changelog|describe' .github/workflows/ci.yml` = no matches. This is the mechanism gap behind the two standin